# thermal-r5prep (29 Sep 2026; docs/android-thermal-20260929.md): PM660 VADC (qcom-spmi-adc5, pm660_adc adc@3100) IIO
# device = the board thermistors the thermal HAL reads (quiet_therm skin, xo/msm/emmc/pa_therm). Same SPMI child naming as
# rom/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts ("800f000.spmi:pmic@0:<node>"). Platform type sysfs_thermal: hal_thermal_default already
# reads it (hal_thermal_a6l.te), no new type. To confirm on the phone: readlink -f /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device*
genfscon sysfs /devices/platform/soc@0/800f000.spmi/spmi-0/0-00/800f000.spmi:pmic@0:adc@3100 u:object_r:sysfs_thermal:s0
# selinux-20261007 (firmware/extracted/selinux-20261007/README.md, group G2): this tree's system/sepolicy no longer labels
# the thermal class devices, so every thermal_zoneN/{type,temp} and cooling_deviceN/{max,cur}_state was generic sysfs
# (r11: hal_thermal_default sysfs:file read x69, logged once per permission). hal_thermal_a6l.te already reads sysfs_thermal.
genfscon sysfs /devices/virtual/thermal                                    u:object_r:sysfs_thermal:s0
